This is the folder for the Student Seaglider Center's 2026 Shilshole test. 
Glider 195 was deployed in Shilshole Bay, Puget Sound on November 20th 2026 and retrieved on November 20th 2026.

This folder contains the mission plan and inside each subfolder, sg194 & sg195, there is the respective meta data file.

The clean_data folder has csv and netCDF files that are corrected for the time offset and fewer renamed variables for simplicity in plotting. The raw data can still be found in raw_files > nc_files > the last file titled  sg195_November_2026_Shilshole_Test_timeseries.nc
The clean_data folder also has csv and netCDF files for the depth averaged currents and finally a python script detailing the process for cleaning the data.

The raw_files folder has all the raw files that come off the basestation. These are sorted by file type. 

For any questions about this mission please contact the Mission PI, Katie Kohlman (kohlman@uw.edu), or the Data Manager, Sophie Monterola (somont@uw.edu).

